<title>JAPAN: Japan August gold imports down 54.1 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan August gold imports down 54.1 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gold imports in August were down 54.1 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			  Aug 96     July 96     Aug 95</p>
<p> Total		   9.53	11.97	  20.74</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Australia	     1.55	 3.90	   5.83</p>
<p> South Africa	  3.14	 2.94	   2.08</p>
<p> Britain		 1.04	 1.52	   3.80</p>
<p> Canada		  0.21	 0.87	   1.18</p>
<p> South Korea	   1.30	 0.80	   0.90</p>
<p> Switzerland	   0.77	 0.76	   3.90</p>
<p>Gold imports in the first eight months of 1996 totalled 105.08 tonnes against 199.47 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
